Overlay patch 0019 rev5 (rebased for LUS c151cc91): harden Metal texture
uploads — clamp, null-guard, exact byte ledger. The rev3/rev4 GENERATED-MIP
machinery (gsIosWantMips heuristic + deferred EndFrame GPU blit) is RETIRED:
upstream c151cc91 grew its own auto-mipmap system (08bb8748..c345b7a5) that
supersedes it and is better — CPU alpha-weighted box pyramids with
alpha-test coverage preservation, keyed on mImportIsHd (the actual
HD-replacement import path, not a dimension heuristic), palette-indexed
textures excluded (averaging indices is meaningless — our GPU blit would
have averaged them), uploaded per-level via UploadTextureMip, sampled
trilinear+aniso via the auto_mipmaps flag (0029 rev2 bumps upstream's
aniso 8 to the D12-measured 16). What remains here, on BOTH upload paths
(UploadTextureMip now carries every HD/pack texture — it is the hot path):
- clamp oversized uploads to GetMaxTextureSize (Metal ABORTS past the
  limit; ImportTextureRaw's OOB-load fallback produces 65536x1 strips,
  which still route through UploadTexture since height<=1 is excluded
  from upstream's automipmaps);
- null-guard newTexture under memory pressure (unchecked replaceRegion
  dereferenced null; stale texels beat a crash);
- exact GPU byte ledger via allocatedSize (feeds 0020's byte-budget
  eviction; mip-aware by construction).

